+
+This is an explicitly authorized isolated workflow experiment, not a real customer project. Work only inside this application and the explicitly supplied skill resources. Do not inspect sibling evaluator material, home credentials or unrelated repositories. Do not install dependencies, commit, publish, use external services or modify global configuration. Prefix shell commands with rtk (rtk proxy for exact output). Use only scenario MCP for workflow YAML; no direct reads/parsers/edits. Preserve unrelated.txt exactly. Use the selected workflow for the requested stage and stop at its boundary. Native question replies come from the frozen simulated respondent and apply only to this fixture. Do not infer additional authorization from them.
+
+The installed client sandbox cannot capture Node child output through its default pipes. Use the existing test-process.mjs runCli(args, { env }) helper for real child-process CLI assertions: it captures stdout/stderr through temporary file descriptors and returns actual status/signal. Preserve the helper and exact stream/exit assertions. Do not replace subprocess checks with imports or mocks. npm test uses the installed Node single-file --test-isolation=none driver to avoid runner IPC; preserve this test command. This is test infrastructure shared by both workflow versions, not a product requirement.
